:Title: Lyntin Installation Document
:Author: Will

VERSION
=======

$Id: INSTALL,v 1.9 2002/07/21 17:37:05 willhelm Exp $

For more up-to-date documentation, check out the web-site at:
http://lyntin.sourceforge.net/



SUMMARY
=======

This file holds installation instructions for Lyntin.  It should be
revisited and re-written at some point.



UNIX/LINUX
==========

1. Make sure you have at least Python 2.2--you can do this by 
   running "python" and seeing what version it says it is.  If 
   you don't have Python 2.2 or later installed, Lyntin won't work.
2. Download the version of Lyntin you're looking for (below) 
3. Untar the client into ~/lyntin or something along those lines
4. Run ``python lyntin.py``

lyntin.py takes a series of options.  For a list of options 
and explanations, run::

   python lyntin.py --help



WINDOWS
=======

1. Make sure you have at least Python 2.2
2. Unzip the client into c:\lyntin
3. Right click on lyntin.py and select ``Create Shortcut``
4. Then right click on the new shortcut and select ``Properties``
5. There are many versions of Windows and I think shortcut properties
   differ between them.  On Win2k, I have my shortcut set up like this:

::

   Target:    {path_to_python}\pythonw.exe c:\lyntin\lyntin.py --ui tk
   Start in:  c:\lyntin
   Run:       Normal window
